#
# What must not reach a build context. Two reasons, and the second is the
# one that bites: sending gigabytes of node_modules is merely slow, but
# copying a *host-built* node_modules or virtual environment into an
# image produces one that was assembled from somebody's desk rather than
# from this repository — and it works, right up until it is built
# somewhere else.

.git
.github

# Host-built dependency trees and their output
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python by-products
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info

# Tool caches
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.cache
**/.turbo

# Editors, OS, local settings
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/*.swp
.claude
CLAUDE.local.md
